      "fp_details": [
        {
          "sentence": 20,
          "component": "HTML5 Client",
          "source": "entity",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "This means that bbb-html5 could use multiple CPU cores for processing messages and handling browser sessions (each nodej"
        },
        {
          "sentence": 21,
          "component": "HTML5 Client",
          "source": "entity",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "As of 2.3-alpha-7, bbb-html5 uses 2 \"frontend\" and two \"backend\" processes (this value is configurable in bbb-html5-with"
        },
        {
          "sentence": 24,
          "component": "HTML5 Client",
          "source": "llmrouter",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Frontends receive the ValidateAuthTokenResp event to complete authentication."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 25,
          "component": "HTML5 Client",
          "source": "llmrouter",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Frontends collect subscriptions and publishers."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 26,
          "component": "HTML5 Client",
          "source": "llmrouter",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Frontends receive other DDP events including method calls to send events to akka-apps."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 27,
          "component": "HTML5 Client",
          "source": "llmrouter",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Frontends handle completely the Streamer redis events, i.e., Cursor, Annotations, External video share."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 28,
          "component": "HTML5 Client",
          "source": "llmrouter",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Frontends still require MeetingStarted and MeetingEnded events to create/destroy per-meeting event processing queues."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 29,
          "component": "HTML5 Server",
          "source": "llmrouter",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Backends handle all the non-streamer events."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 30,
          "component": "HTML5 Server",
          "source": "llmrouter",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "If more than one backend is running, bbb-web splits the load in round-robin fashion by assigning an instanceId."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 31,
          "component": "HTML5 Server",
          "source": "llmrouter",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "So individual backends only process redis events for the meetings matching the associated instanceId."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 32,
          "component": "HTML5 Server",
          "source": "llmrouter",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "ValidateAuthTokenResp is passed to backends as well, which is needed for the cases where you only have a backend, no fro"
        },
        {
          "sentence": 50,
          "component": "Recording Service",
          "source": "llmrouter",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "When the meeting ends, the Recording Processor will take all the recorded events as well as the different raw (PDF, WAV,"
        },
        {
          "sentence": 58,
          "component": "FSESL",
          "source": "coreference",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "We have extracted out the component that integrates with FreeSWITCH into it\u2019s own application."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 76,
          "component": "Presentation Conversion",
          "source": "entity",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Uploaded presentations go through a conversion process in order to be displayed inside the client."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 79,
          "component": "Presentation Conversion",
          "source": "entity",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "The conversion process sends progress messages to the client through the Redis pubsub."
        }
      ],
